{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 71, :comments ["<b>After the suckling-lambs</b> — an adjective resembling a verb, on the pattern of עולים; regarding sheep, the עולות are the females." "<b>To shepherd</b> — with an additional bet, like 'shepherding his brothers among the sheep.' Now at first he shepherded sheep, and he returned to shepherd Israel, as he began at the start of the psalm: 'and He led His people like sheep.'" "<b>And the sense of 'and with skill of His hands He guides them'</b> — because He likened the people of HaShem to sheep, and a good shepherd is needed, and everything with a staff, therefore 'and with skill.' And in my opinion: the bet in תבונות serves two, like 'and His arm upon them,' as if written: 'and with the skill of His hands He guides them.' Now the sense of 'according to the entirety of His heart' — to do good for His people, and 'with the skill of His hands' — that is the deed, as it is written: 'and David performed justice and righteousness for all his people.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:26.778296209Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}